# scripts/github-bootstrap.sh creates both teams and gives them their roles.
#
# This file requests the right reviewer. Requiring the approval is the rulesets'
# job, not this file's; the rulesets on main also require two approvals from
# @guardana/security-maintainers on the authorization paths among those below,
# listed in scripts/lib/github-settings.sh. Who has to approve what is in
# GOVERNANCE.md.
#
# Last matching pattern wins, so the specific paths below override the
# catch-all above them.

*                      @guardana/maintainers

# Paths that carry authorization meaning: the decision path, the enforcement
# pipeline, the approvals store, the policy keys, the digest an approval binds
# to, the evidence record, contract validation, the judgement of a run against
# its procedure, the route and lift signatures and the stop judge, the commands
# that sign a route, turn findings into stops and start, list, carry and lift a
# stop list, the plane's reading of its route, the reading of a run's evidence
# for supervision, the runs directory and the findings log, the policy and
# route floors and their refresh, the owner and mode checks of the configuration
# and of every store, the external decision point's answer, which may only veto,
# the MCP adapter, which classifies a tool, sends only the authorized bytes under
# their obligations, names the run a call belongs to and withholds or rewrites
# answers, the policy provider interface, the wire schema and the fixtures that
# pin them. Every tree scripts/lib/dependency-rule.sh guards is among them.
/internal/core/        @guardana/security-maintainers
/internal/policy/      @guardana/security-maintainers
/internal/canon/       @guardana/security-maintainers
/internal/evidence/    @guardana/security-maintainers
/internal/supervise/   @guardana/security-maintainers
/internal/gateway/     @guardana/security-maintainers
/internal/approvals/   @guardana/security-maintainers
/internal/policykey/   @guardana/security-maintainers
/internal/reaction/    @guardana/security-maintainers
/internal/policystate/ @guardana/security-maintainers
/internal/gatewayconfig/ @guardana/security-maintainers
/internal/files/       @guardana/security-maintainers
/internal/policywatch/ @guardana/security-maintainers
/internal/runs/        @guardana/security-maintainers
/internal/findinglog/  @guardana/security-maintainers
/cmd/guardana-control/route*.go @guardana/security-maintainers
/cmd/guardana-control/react*.go @guardana/security-maintainers
/cmd/guardana-control/stops.go @guardana/security-maintainers
/cmd/guardana-control/supervise_input.go @guardana/security-maintainers
/cmd/guardana-gateway/reaction.go @guardana/security-maintainers
/cmd/guardana-gateway/pdp.go @guardana/security-maintainers
/cmd/guardana-gateway/adapter.go @guardana/security-maintainers
/cmd/guardana-gateway/build.go @guardana/security-maintainers
/cmd/guardana-gateway/approvals.go @guardana/security-maintainers
/cmd/guardana-gateway/serve.go @guardana/security-maintainers
/cmd/guardana-gateway/stop.go @guardana/security-maintainers
/adapters/authzen/     @guardana/security-maintainers
/adapters/mcp/         @guardana/security-maintainers
/adapters/enforce/     @guardana/security-maintainers
/internal/adapterkit/  @guardana/security-maintainers
/pkg/contract/         @guardana/security-maintainers
/pkg/policyprovider/   @guardana/security-maintainers
/api/proto/            @guardana/security-maintainers
/testdata/             @guardana/security-maintainers

# The gate those paths are held to, and what it is built from. A change here
# can drop a check or a linter, weaken the breaking-change rule or add a
# dependency without touching a line of the decision path. /.golangci.* covers
# every name golangci-lint reads as its configuration, not only the one
# `make lint` passes to it.
/Makefile              @guardana/security-maintainers
/.golangci.*           @guardana/security-maintainers
/buf.yaml              @guardana/security-maintainers
/buf.gen.yaml          @guardana/security-maintainers
/go.mod                @guardana/security-maintainers
/go.sum                @guardana/security-maintainers
/scripts/              @guardana/security-maintainers
/internal/testreport/  @guardana/security-maintainers
/internal/docscheck/   @guardana/security-maintainers
/.github/              @guardana/security-maintainers
/.goreleaser.yaml      @guardana/security-maintainers
# The Python client's project file, lock, build constraints and the two
# programs its gate target runs: what the client is tested with and built
# from. Its sources and tests below src/ and tests/ are reviewed like any
# source.
/clients/python/*      @guardana/security-maintainers

# The normative pages. A spec change is a contract change: the wire contract
# page and everything under docs/spec/ are reviewed as the schema is.
/docs/contracts.md     @guardana/security-maintainers
/docs/spec/            @guardana/security-maintainers
